          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            An
            %strong
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
              \-coproduct
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit+in+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} colimit in an (∞,1)-category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            over a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagram"} diagram
            of the shape
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi A
                  %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo →
                  %mi 𝒞
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\{A \quad B\} \to \mathcal{C}
                  \\,.
          %p
            In other words it is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocone"} cocone
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi A
                  %mo ⊔
                  %mi B
                  %mo ←
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \to A \sqcup B \leftarrow B
            which is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+property"} universal
            among all such cocones in the
            = succeed "-categorical" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
          %p
            This is the analog in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+theory"} (∞,1)-category theory
            of the notion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproduct"} coproduct
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+theory"} category theory
